# WebTransport interop peers (WT-196).
#
# This file exists so the port-80 Caddy obtains and renews the Let's Encrypt
# certificate that the interop peers serve on their QUIC ports. The peers are
# not HTTP services, so the site itself only answers a status line.
#
# Caddy's default EC key. An RSA certificate was tried on 16 September 2026 to
# see whether the erlang quicer peer needed one; it made the other four peers
# fail, so the erlang trust failure is not a key-type problem and this is back
# to the default.
pummelchen.91.99.176.243.nip.io {
	respond "WebTransport interop host" 200
}
